# Open an exact regional tour

Guided learning catalogue rows offer **Open tour** for a currently admitted
regional tour. The link names its exact tour revision and learner-source
revision. It opens the existing 3D Atlas with that tour selected, not playing.
Choose Start or Play when the viewer has admitted its source models.

The catalogue retains its canonical region metadata. Tour intents use the
shared `/atlas/3d` workspace with an explicit region; ordinary navigation still
uses the existing dedicated regional pages. The native links do not prefetch,
start playback, move an already mounted camera or create a new message channel.
Use normal browser Back/Forward for page history. Existing unsaved-work guards
and independent content access remain unchanged.

Only bounded public tour ID, tour revision, source revision and region fields
are transported. Duplicate, partial, malformed and mixed study/head-tour
requests are refused. The embedded source validates the exact tour, source,
region, targets and every camera frame again. An obsolete link selects nothing;
it never silently substitutes the first tour. A model/renderer must be ready
and the learner must explicitly start playback. Mount-only initialization
cannot replace later user selection or active study/practice/guided activity.

When an old catalogue lacks a usable direct-entry revision, its clearly labelled
manual region link remains available only for a canonical destination. Invalid
destinations are not turned into links. No arbitrary URL, private identifier,
scan, quiz answer, permission or autoplay value is forwarded.

This applies to the existing regional-tour registry, including Whole body's
declared same-catalogue union. Separate specimen/nested guides and the shoulder
reference module retain their own interfaces; no universal coverage is claimed.
Teaching remains draft. Semantic anatomy comparison is not patient-space
registration, and Atlas access does not grant separately paid lectures or cases.

Original MIT application code/prose. No new asset, dependency, model, dataset,
font, texture, service or fee. Existing source notices and holds are retained.
The candidate remains unpublished and uninstalled until the owner chooses to
change the normal preview. Validation receipts distinguish native/source/build
proofs from browser, authentication, clinical and release acceptance.
